    "body": "\r\n\r\n## Problem\r\n\r\nWindows CI fails since f83acfd327e3756c65f69f170055fe18a751f5f2 : the `:grep` test greps the contents of `test/*`, which depends on whatever is in the test files. After that commit, quickfix expands `\"$⨯\"` in diagnostic_spec.lua as part of a file name, which logs an error:\r\n\r\n    $NVIM_LOG_FILE: D:/a/neovim/neovim/build/nvim.log_ex_cmds\r\n    ERR 2026-09-30T17:34:03.034 T190.2776.0 os_getenv:98: uv_os_getenv(�) failed: -4071 EINVAL\r\n\r\n## Analysis\r\n\r\n`expand_env_esc()` has buggy logic: it reads the name bytewise (not UTF8-aware), so `expand_env(\"$é\")` looks up `\"\\xC3\"`.\r\n\r\n    while (c-- > 0 && *tail != NUL && vim_isIDc((uint8_t)(*tail))) {\r\n      *var++ = *tail++;\r\n    }\r\n\r\n## Solution\r\n\r\nIn the `:grep` test, grep test/functional/fixtures/bigfile.txt instead of the entire `test/*` contents. This is faster and more predictable.\r\n",
    "closed_at": "2026-10-01T11:29:43Z",
